@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] production-crate-and-native-host
Code in this subtree MUST remain in the production `advanced-show-control` crate rooted at `app/`.
The production desktop host and presentation layer MUST use GPUI under `native_ui`; a web frontend,
Tauri host, or JavaScript command/event bridge MUST NOT be reintroduced.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] actor-owned-state-boundaries
Production code outside a domain owner MUST request state changes through that owner's explicit
command interface or documented synchronous API. It MUST NOT mutate actor-owned state directly or
move business validation into handles or native UI adapters.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] runtime-events-are-facts
Production `AppEventBus` events MUST report facts that have occurred, never request work. Requests
MUST use the owning domain's command interface, and diagnostics that do not represent application
state MUST use `tracing` instead of the event bus.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:safety] generation-scoped-stale-work
Code holding shared generation authority MUST treat a rejected generation check as terminal for the
operation. It MUST NOT then send LV1 commands, mutate current or app-lifetime state, or publish or
log success, and stale work MUST NOT affect a newer runtime.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] generation-tagged-fact-filtering
Generation-scoped LV1 and Fade actors MAY publish facts without reading shared generation authority,
but every such fact MUST carry the actor's assigned generation. Consumers of generation-bound state
MUST discard facts that do not match their active generation.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] projector-only-frontend-state
The projector MUST be the only backend component that constructs `AppViewState` snapshots and MUST
publish them through its host-neutral latest-value sink. Native UI adapters MAY forward complete
snapshots into GPUI presentation state but MUST NOT construct snapshots or implement domain policy.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:architecture] backend-snapshot-authority
Production backend-owned UI state MUST enter GPUI presentation state through complete projector
snapshots. Production snapshot consumers MUST apply a snapshot only when its `state_version` is
newer than the latest accepted version; command results MUST NOT overwrite newer projected state.
Development-only smoke tooling MAY observe snapshots directly for test orchestration.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:safety] frontend-safety-is-advisory
Native UI visibility, disabled states, and confirmation controls MAY prevent accidental requests,
but MUST NOT enforce lockout, generation, freshness, or exact-scene safety. Those decisions MUST
remain authoritative in the owning application domains.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:product] settings-full-replacement
Each production settings edit MUST dispatch one complete `AppSettings` replacement through the
application command context. Production presentation code MUST NOT send partial settings values or
treat command completion as an authoritative projected update. A transient complete-object draft
MAY be displayed while awaiting the next projector snapshot.

@cc [owner:mixxorz,label:security;logging] diagnostic-data-minimization
Production tracing and UI-safe errors MUST NOT include credentials, tokens, raw OSC payloads, or
serialized or debug-formatted `AppSettings`, `PersistedSettings`, `ShowFile`, or `SessionDocument`
values. User-facing messages MUST remain understandable without structured diagnostic fields.
